      "reader": "reader-b",
      "id": "Q82",
      "path": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/spirit-island/2026-11-05-batch-002957/expanded-iteration-08/adjudication-01/raw-cases.json",
      "json_pointer": "/readers/reader-b/answers/1/evidence/0/text",
      "text": "No real Damage is marked, so different Powers or a Repeat cannot combine their hypothetical Damage; multiple instructions **within one Power** can."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-b",
      "id": "Q82",
      "path": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/spirit-island/2026-11-05-batch-002957/expanded-iteration-08/adjudication-01/raw-cases.json",
      "json_pointer": "/readers/reader-b/answers/1/answer",
      "text": "Separate Powers cannot combine Bringer\u2019s hypothetical Damage: 2 Damage and then separate 1 Damage do not destroy the undamaged City or earn Fear. If 2 then 1 are instructions within one Power, they can combine to hypothetically destroy it, earning 5 Fear and pushing it. A Repeat can pretend-destroy the same piece again for Fear."
